From 8ec420c428a5eadbcb00a8828a657b82d22db711 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: openEuler RISC-V Maintainers <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 12:30:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] arguments: do not use input as a format string

The custom resolution is user-controlled data, not a printf format.
Copy it through a literal format so the code is safe and builds with
openEuler's format-security hardening.
---
 main.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/main.c b/main.c
index ef178d2..a72f2de 100644
--- a/main.c
+++ b/main.c
@@ -124 +124 @@ int arguments(const int argc, char* argv[], int a)
-            snprintf(monitor_res, sizeof(monitor_res), optarg);
+            snprintf(monitor_res, sizeof(monitor_res), "%s", optarg);
